# cp .env.example .env, then fill in. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# Every value here is OPTIONAL. Absent is a supported mode: the stack comes up
# on loopback with delivery falling back to the Beacon incident record, which is
# a degradation you can see rather than a failure that stops the plane starting.
#
# Nothing in this file is read by a container directly. `up.sh` reads it and
# writes the two secret FILES that Prometheus and Alertmanager mount, because a
# credential in an environment variable is a credential in `docker inspect`, in
# every crash dump and in the process table.

# --- Grafana ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The one interactive credential this stack holds. Grafana is bound to
# 127.0.0.1:9091 so the exposure is an operator on the host, but "only reachable
# on loopback" is not a password policy.
#
# REQUIRED since 2026-08-09. The compose file spells it `:?` and no longer
# carries a default, so an unset variable stops the render rather than choosing
# a password for you. Generate one and keep it here:
#
#   od -An -tx1 -N24 /dev/urandom | tr -d ' \n'
CF_GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# --- Beacon scrape ---------------------------------------------------------
# Beacon gates /metrics behind auth (infra/beacon/src/server.js:373) and accepts
# a static break-glass token in an `x-beacon-token` header. It is EMPTY on the
# running estate today, which means the scrape 401s until somebody sets
# BEACON_TOKEN in the estate's own .env and the SAME value here.
#
# AD-20 says adopting a scraper "costs a scrape config rather than a rewrite".
# It costs a scrape config AND this — which is the correct design (an open
# /metrics publishes the shape of the estate to anyone who can reach the port)
# but it is one step more than the decision record predicts.
CF_BEACON_TOKEN=

# --- Alert delivery --------------------------------------------------------
# Where a page goes, and where a ticket goes. Both fall back to Beacon's
# incident receiver when unset.
#
# The estate's existing BEACON_WEBHOOK_URL is kept as the CHAT receiver and is
# explicitly not the paging path: paging needs acknowledgement and escalation,
# and a fire-and-forget POST has neither.
CF_PAGE_WEBHOOK_URL=
CF_TICKET_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- Compose ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Change only if you run two copies of this stack on one host, which nothing
# here is designed for.
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=cfmicro
